description:
Hi team,

Could you please help with the below issue for ABB: The text is being
automatically moved to the next page though there is space on the 1st page.
CC'ed is our partner Synaptic's developer Bart who is working with ABB.

When I generate a PDF with a table, where a cell has a long text content
(plain text, no HTML), the text seems to be cut in the middle of the page,
and moved to the new page (see attached image).

My table HTML is generated in APEX. Please find the table HTML in the
screenshot below. I'm also attaching some CSS that I'm using.


My css:

table.y-stable {
  width: 98%;
  table-layout: fixed;
  font-family: sans-serif;
  font-size: 12px;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  /*page-break-inside:avoid;*/
  border-spacing: 0;
  border: none;
  margin-left: 1px;
  margin-right: 1px;
}


.y-stable td, th {
  padding: 6px 4px;
  vertical-align: top;
  border: 1px solid #000;
  page-break-inside: avoid !important;
  break-inside: avoid !important;
  }



-- 
Thanks,
Sharath Christy
